    "media:imagetext": "SAN FRANCISCO\nDong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and painting\nthe beautiful, the monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than forty\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad\nSAN FRANCISCO the city on the bay, is a favorite of everyone. From Grant Avenue, in the heart of\nChinatown, with its Festivals, to Nob Hill, Fisherman's Wharf or the Golden Gate Bridge, there is so\nmuch to see. The quaint Cable Cars and other historical attractions blend with fine restaurants.\nelegant stores, and famous hotels such as Inter-Continental's renowned Mark Hopkins, to create a\nunique atmosphere. Pan Am serves San Francisco every day from New York, Houston, Miami,\nCentral and South America, Hawaii, Tokyo, Hong Kong, and London. In fact, you can get to\nSan Francisco on Pan Am from just about any place in the world.\nNAM.\n2001.080.247∞",
